BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Comprehensive Lathe Apr 26 [Sundays 6 Week Intensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260426T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260426T170000
UID:ttl-10955828592833@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for those wishing to advance their skil
 ls from novice on a wood lathe. Class sizes are small so you will get a lo
 t of time on one of our multiple lathes. Projects will range from small fo
 untain pens\, progressing to bowls and platters with an emphasis on safety
 . \n\n The TTL Makerspace is a thriving community of like minded makers an
 d the perfect place to develop a foundation in shop safety and etiquette. 
 We will try to spend most of the class on the lathe with students taking t
 urns on our different machines. \n\n Schedule: \n\n Six three-hour weekly 
 classes\, Sundays 2pm to 5pm \n\n Outcomes: \n\n At the end of this course
  you will have experienced the following: \n\n \n- Complete understanding 
 of the anatomy of a lathe \n\n- Experience with a variety of turning tools
  \n\n- Use of an array of lathe accessories \n\n- Preparation of blanks \n
 \n- Use of mandrels and inserts \n\n- Experience with a variety of woods \
 n\n- Turning spindles \n\n- Turning bowls and platters \n\n \n \n\n Follow
 ing the course\, you’ll be able to use both Craftex and Coronet Herald l
 athes at TTLMakerspace with your active membership. And you’ll be able t
 o join the active group of Makers sharing knowledge in our Discord communi
 ty. \n\n Useful for: pens\, spindles\, bowls\, platters \n\n Want to get n
 otified next time classes are posted? \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/comprehensive-lathe-apr-26-sundays-6-we
 ek-intensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pen Wood Turning Workshop - Apr 19
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260419T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260419T170000
UID:ttl-10955824693441@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Pens have become so popular around the Makerspace that we've d
 ecided to run a workshop to teach others how to make them too! \n \n \n\n 
 \n \n \n 4 Lathes\, 4 Participants\, 3 Hours of wood-turning fun! Best of 
 all you get to take home your very own handmade wooden pen. \n \n \n\n \n 
 \n \n We will cover: \n\n \n \n \n \n- Safe operation of a lathe. \n\n- Cr
 eating a wooden pen blank. \n\n- Setting up the machine. \n\n- Turning a P
 en! \n\n \n \n \n \n Note: No woodworking experience is required. You must
  have short sleeves\, flat closed toes shoes and have long hair tied back.
  Personal safety equipment will be supplied. Pen kits may not match the pi
 ctures used for this class.
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/pen-wood-turning-workshop-apr-19
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Depth Leathercraft Intro - May 7 [Thursdays - 6 week program]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T210000
UID:ttl-10955811094721@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Leatherworking at TTLMakerspace \n\n \n \n \n \n \n Learn the 
 basics of leather working at the TTL Makerspace in a small hands-on class 
 where we will study traditional as well as modern methods of working with 
 leather.\n\n \n \n \n \n Small class sizes will allow you to get the guida
 nce needed to get you making leather projects with confidence. You will ta
 ke home 4 creations of your own design and if you cant get enough in class
 \, you can use the TTL Makerspace leatherworking kits or borrow one of the
  Toronto Tool Library’s similar kits.\n\n Materials and equipment for al
 l projects are provided with the course.\n\n \n \n \n Projects: \n \n Proj
 ect 1: Leather Wallet \n Project 2: Coin Purse \n Project 3: Waterskin \n 
 Project 4: Collar/bracelet \n \n \n Materials and equipment for all projec
 ts are provided with the course. \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n Schedule \n6 
 weeks\, Thursdays 6pm to 9pm \n \n \n\n \n \n Outcomes \n At the end of th
 e course you will have achieved the following goals: \n \n  \n\n \n- A go
 od understanding of the nature and properties of leather \n\n- A solid fou
 ndation in various methods of cutting\, burnishing\, dying and finishing. 
 \n\n- Experience with stamping and engraving leather projects. \n\n- Famil
 iarity with sewing machines and their use on thinner leather. \n\n- Knowle
 dge of wet molding and the waterproofing of leather. \n\n- An understandin
 g of studs\, buckles\, rivets\, snaps and other hardware. \n\n \n \n \n \n
 \n \n Useful for: bags\, garments\, belts\, custom cases/sheaths
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/in-depth-leathercraft-intro-may-7-thurs
 days-6-week-program
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In-Depth Intro to Woodworking May 28 [Thursdays - 6 week Intensive
 ]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T130000
UID:ttl-10955806310593@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Woodworking at TTLMakerspace\n\n \n Suitable for beginners\, t
 his woodworking course is designed to teach you all that you need to get s
 tarted in woodworking by learning both traditional\, and modern techniques
 .\n\n Students will learn valuable hands-on skills working on instructor-l
 ead projects using both hand and power tools.\n\n Projects are chosen to p
 rovide skills development in a natural progression from familiarity with t
 he unique characteristics of wood\, to basic essential techniques\, to som
 e more advanced topics.\n\n Materials and equipment for all projects are p
 rovided with the course.\n\n \n\n Schedule : \n\n Six three-hour weekly cl
 asses\, Thursdays 10am to 1pm. \n\n Outcomes : \n\n At the end of this co
 urse you will have achieved the following goals: \n\n \n- A complete under
 standing of the nature and properties of wood \n\n- Proficiency with tradi
 tional woodworking techniques\n\n- Comfort working with chisels\, planes\,
  saws\n\n- Proficiency with wood milling techniques\n\n- Comfort with saf
 e operation of power tools\n\n- Familiarity with power planing\, joiner\, 
 drill press\, router and table saw \n\n- Dressing and laminating wood \n\n
 - Experience following project plans \n\n- Familiarity with joinery \n\n-
  Wood finishing\, various treatments \n\n \n  Following this course\, you
 'll be certified to use the woodshop. And you'll be able to join the growi
 ng community of TTL Makers sharing knowledge on our Discord community.\n\n
  Certifications for all courses are valid for one year from the time that 
 they are issued\, and can be renewed at no cost with your active monthly m
 embership within 3 months of their expiry. Certification renewal requires 
 booking with an instructor\, is conducted at the makerspace\, and helps yo
 u keep your skills current. \n\nUseful for: furniture\, cabinets\, organi
 sers\, cutting-boards \n \n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes a
 re posted? \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/in-depth-intro-to-woodworking-may-28-th
 ursdays-6-week-intensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Designing for Lasers - May 30 [Saturdays 6 week comprehensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T170000
UID:ttl-10955801755841@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:In this course at TTLMakerspace\, you will go from beginner to
  practical working knowledge of designing and modelling in 2D and 3D\, and
  the operation of a laser for etching and cutting a variety of materials. 
 \n\n Starting with desktop versions of lasers you’ll work your way throu
 gh lessons and projects up to the industrial ThunderLaser cutter. \n\n Out
 comes: \n\n At the end of this course you will have achieved the following
  goals: \n\n \n- A complete understanding of the steps needed to go from c
 oncept to completed project \n\n- Familiarity with the properties of a var
 iety of materials - woods\, plastics\, textiles \n\n- Experience and compr
 ehension of the most important principles of CAD modelling for constructin
 g with laser cut parts \n\n- Setting speeds and power levels \n\n- Creatin
 g a design environment and workflow \n\n- Full understanding of the most c
 ommon etching and cutting operations \n\n- Experience creating tool paths 
 with Lightburn software \n\n- Setting up materials and performing operatio
 ns \n\n- Machine maintenance and Safety \n\n \n Schedule: 6 lessons\, Satu
 rdays\, 2pm-5pm \n\n Following this course\, you’ll be certified to use 
 desktop lasers\, and book time with the industrial laser at TTLMakerspace 
 (with your membership). You will also be able to join the growing communit
 y of TTL Makers sharing Laser knowledge on our Discord community. \n\n Use
 ful for : signs\, gifts\, personalising anything\, stamp-making\, organise
 r\, decorative items\, lanterns \n\n Want to get notified next time classe
 s are posted? \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/designing-for-lasers-may-30-saturdays-6
 -week-comprehensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CNC Milling for Builders - May 21  [Thursdays - 6 Week Comprehensi
 ve]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T210000
UID:ttl-10955798413505@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:CNC for Builders \n\n \n \n\n \n In this course at TTLMakerspa
 ce\, you will go from beginner to a practical working knowledge of CAD mod
 elling and CNC machining with an automated milling machine\, specifically 
 for furniture\, cabinetry\, frames etc. \n \n \n \n \n \n Starting with de
 sktop versions of CNC machines\, you’ll work your way through lessons up
  to the industrial Omni 1350 6’ x 8’ CNC milling machine. \n \n \n\n \
 n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Schedule : \n \n \n Six three-hour weekly classe
 s\, Thursdays 6pm to 9pm. \n \n \n \n \n \n Outcomes : \n \n \n At the end
  of this course you will have achieved the following goals: \n \n \n- \n A
  complete understanding of the steps needed to go from concept to complete
 d part \n\n- \n Familiarity with the properties of a variety of hardwood m
 aterials \n\n- \n Experience and comprehension of the most important princ
 iples of CAD modelling \n\n- \n Selecting and programming the most commonl
 y used tools \n\n- \n Full understanding of the most common machining oper
 ations \n\n- \n Experience creating tool paths with CAM software \n\n- \n 
 Setting up a CNC mill and performing operations \n\n- \n Machine maintenan
 ce and Safety \n\n \n \n Following this course\, you’ll be certified to 
 use desktop mills\, and book time with the industrial mill at TTLMakerspac
 e (with your membership). You will also be able to join the growing commun
 ity of TTL Makers sharing CNC knowledge on our Discord community. \n \n \n
  \n \n \n Useful for: furniture\, cabinets\, flat-pack\, desktops\, boats\
 , frames \n \n \n\n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes are poste
 d? \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/cnc-milling-for-builders-may-21-thursda
 ys-6-week-comprehensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
